Power includes military strength and influence. Support is weighted by projected rebel participation and court mood. An undecided player vassal is uncommitted.

The Crown of {REALM} will pass to {HEIR}. {HEIR} will found the ruling house of {HOUSE}. An eligible spouse may accompany them; existing children will remain in their current clan.

Inheritance granted now:
{FIEFS}
Legal titles: {TITLES}
Gold: {GOLD}

{REGENCY}
You will continue as {RULER}, leading your original clan. The rest of your treasury remains yours. This inheritance is granted now, not again upon your death. Continue?

The Crown of {REALM} will pass to {HEIR} of {HOUSE}.

{REGENCY}
You will retain your character, original clan, estates and treasury. Continue?

New cadet house: {HOUSE}
Fiefs: {FIEFS}
Titles: {TITLES}
Gold: {GOLD}

Goodwill toward the Crown prompted this undertaking.
Intended recipients: {TARGETS}
Scheduled for {DATE}.

Discontent with the Crown prompted this undertaking.
Intended recipients: {TARGETS}
Scheduled for {DATE}.

{MOTION}

Selection costs {COST} influence. Filing costs {FILING} influence at the appointed session on {DATE}.

{DETAIL}

Facing defeat at the hands of {THREAT}, {RULER} offers to place {CLIENT} under your protection as a client kingdom. In return, they ask you to take up their defense against {THREAT}.

Acceptance commits you and your client states to that conflict, unless already engaged. The new client will follow your foreign policy and join your wars; its unrelated independent wars and foreign agreements will be settled under the ordinary terms of clientage.

{BALANCE}

The nobility asks you to bestow {TITLE} upon {RECIPIENT}, recognizing that house's claim. Will you grant their petition?

Rights: {RIGHTS}
Cost: 100 influence
Personal goodwill: +{RELATION}
Recipient faction approval: +{APPROVAL}

The house remains your vassal. No subordinate settlement changes owner. A grant fulfills the petition without a second approval reward. You may reconsider before {DATE}; leaving the petition unfulfilled brings -10 approval.

{MOTION}

Cost: {COST} influence.

{DETAIL}

Your peers will entrust this matter to your judgment. Bring one proposal before the court by {DATE}, or they will remember your unfulfilled promise.

{ACTION}

Substitution costs {COST} influence. The usual proposal cost is paid only when you file; deliberation begins then.

{DESCRIPTION}

{COMPETENCE}
{REQUIREMENTS}
Personal competence before council-wide bonuses. Skills count up to 300 and attributes up to 10.
